  "data_abstract": "Three-particle azimuthal correlation measurements with a high transverse momentum trigger particle are reported for pp, d+Au, and Au+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 200 GeV by the STAR experiment. Dijet structures are observed in pp, d+Au and peripheral Au+Au collisions. An additional structure is observed in central Au+Au data, signaling conical emission of correlated charged hadrons. The conical emission angle is found to be $\\theta$ = 1.37 $\\pm$ 0.02(stat)$^{+0.06}_{\u22120.07}$(syst), independent of p$_\\perp$.",
  "data_keywords": {
